#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# group_order

#% text
# `group_order(G)`: the number of elements of a permutation or finitely presented group

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For a permutation group the order is the product of the orbit lengths of a stabiliser chain (Schreier-Sims).

#% item
# For a finitely presented group it is the number of cosets of the trivial subgroup (Todd-Coxeter), and `inf` when the abelian invariants show an infinite cyclic factor.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
group_order(mathieu_group(11))
#% output
#= 7920

#% cell
group_order(symmetric_group(30))
#% output
#= 265252859812191058636308480000000

#% cell
group_order(finitely_presented_group([a, b], [a^2, b^3, table([a, b], 5)]))
#% output
#= 60

#% cell
group_order(finitely_presented_group([a, b], [[a, b] -> [b, a]]))
#% output
#= inf

